He already named Iran. The colonel says the real story is the exit.

@MarioNawfal sat Col. Lawrence Wilkerson down as the offer and the hijack landed in the same hour. Wilkerson was Colin Powell’s chief of staff. He has spent twenty years saying the briefings do not match the map. Listen to him before the podium.

Bloomberg’s item is the diplomacy. Araghchi offered IAEA access to the bombed nuclear sites in exchange for easing sanctions. Pezeshkian had already talked about blending down the 60 percent stock, inspectors back in, Iran staying in the NPT, Hormuz reopened in phases if the blockade lifts. Wilkerson’s read is colder. Xi took the temperature in Washington, the visit produced nothing, and Beijing may have told Tehran to lean forward so the refusal lands on Washington. Rubio had already pushed the Iranian delegation out of New York early. An opening you know will be rejected is not weakness. It is a file for the next speech.

Then the plane. A Saudi official told NBC the initial read may include foreign backing. Netanyahu hinted at Iran on a U.S. press tour. The co-pilot was already moved to the UAE. Israel is sending a team. Trump said, on what he is hearing, Iran is involved, and retaliation follows if that holds. Wilkerson calls it a tempest built for the cameras. He does not trust an Israeli-assisted probe. He lived the Rachel Corrie file. His line is that Bibi would stage a pretext, and that any scrap of paper falling out of the sky will be used to hide the actual result: the United States getting its butt kicked out of Southwest Asia for good, with a president sticking a finger in a dyke that will not hold.

The rest is the invoice he says they are lying about. Diesel. Fuel oil. Two-thirds of the country already in recession, the whole country there by the election, depression after. Airplanes come and go. The magazine does not refill because a press hit says so.

This is the man who never stops bragging that he built the greatest military on earth. A five-time draft dodger who never saw combat is spending the last interceptors on a war he does not understand. Bases chewed up. Hormuz still a bargaining chip. He wrecked the force, wrecked the price of diesel, and is dragging the world toward empty shelves.

Watch it. The offer is real. The blame came first.

